  of 8 and 16 bit loads and stores prior to 21164A was a mistake but
  the Alpha scheme for access via pointer with unknown alignment is
  fine (no exceptions, just a few extra instructions).

  Where Apple really screwed its semi partner was when Motorola was
  jumping through hoops for an 88K Mac; Apple insisted the 88100
  support 80 bit FP to be compatible with its SANE package.  Supposedly
  this contributed much to the 88100 schedule slip.  The ironic part
  was Apple jettisoned 88K in favour of PPC and it has no support for
  80 bit FP format.

  Speaking of 80 bit FP; MPR's conjectures on Merced based on Intel
  WIPO patent speculate that IA64 will retain 80 bit FP regs.

--
