On 22 Apr 1997 10:23:01 GMT, Tobias Wildi <wildit> wrote:

>>I've got a 20-inch digital monitor from 1988 (model VR290-D3) and I'd like to
>>connect it to my PC (VGA-card). The monitor has 3 bnc-connectors, but it
>>doesn't work with the 'normal' cable that I bought.
>>Can anybody help me?

	You'd get better results if you posted a valid E-mail address with
your messages. In any case...

	The reason it's not working is because those monitors are
fixed-frequency, sync-on-green, and the sync rates they use are not
compatible with those put out by standard PC video cards.

	It is possible to use such a monitor on a PC, but doing so will
require a specialized (and fairly expensive) video card that is
specifically designed to handle fixed-freq monitors.

	There's a company in Florida, name of Mirage, that makes such. Expect
to pay between USD $150-$200.


