> 
>   As far as I know, the KDA50 is not supported in the BA123. It's supported
> in the H9642 dual-BA23 config and in some S-Box (BA2xx) cabinets.
> 
>   I think this is due to power supply restrictions - there's a worksheet in
> the BA123 owner's manual (and in the manuals for the various systems that
> come in BA123's) for calculating power load. Of course, if you have any 3rd-
> party boards you'll need their data (or good guesses).

If memory serves, the primary reason is because the KDA50 is a
two-board set that has to go into CD slots, instead of ABAB.  If
memory serves, the BA-23 has three such slots, one for the CPU and two
for memory cards.  The standard BA123 has (I think) four such slots.
That would handle 1 CPU, a third-party 16Mbyte board, and a KD-A50.

At least *some* BA123-derived enclosures had sufficient power supply
for a KDA50.  (five CPUs and 128Mbytes of memory easily outconsume
just about anything).



