   Alan,

   I have a PC setup that is pretty good (details on request).  A
   17-inch monitor helps.  But you do need a decent VT emulator.  I
   have tried a fistfull of the shareware ones from Strouds and Tucows
   (the two hot Windows app sites).   IMHO, many of them were little
   more than a joke.  They are getting better, however.  It seems to
   me that most of the authors are rather amateur in their approach to
   full emulation and testing of what they say they emulate.  NONE
   (AFAIK) of them do doublehigh / doublewide characters.  I guess the
   idea is write some junk and get the world to do the preliminary
   debugging for you.  Free labour.

   HOWEVER, PROCOMM does very well with its VT100 emulations.  Until
   something better comes along, Get PROCOMM PLUS 3.0 for Windows. 
   MODEM or TCP/IP TELNET support.  Nice fonts, nice colors (but not
   enough color selection), even over 132 cpl and still highly
   readable, and doublehigh / doublewide characters as well.  PROCOMM
   is the ONLY VTxxx emulator I have found that is passable and that
   seems to do all the escape sequences I throw at it.   It also comes
   with email, ftp (gifs viewable as they download) and web browser
   clients as well as a very powerful scripting language and pretty
   good online help.

