Maybe this is a nit, maybe not...  "Polycenter" covers a lot of things.
All you need is the LSM license to do striping.  That may well be
overpriced, I don't know, but make sure you're looking at the right
license.  We have lots of license packages that may include stuff
you don't need.  The LSM license will get you the GUI and mirroring.

Beyond that you have two choices; software and hardware.

Lots of people make RAID controllers that support striping as well
as RAID-5 and maybe mirroring.  One of those would probably be
more than the $2100 you're trying to save.

I haven't heard of anybody doing a striping driver (*).  If you don't
mind funneling the driver to a single CPU, a striping driver shouldn't
be an especially hard driver.  Though you'll need to figure out how to
manage the disk label correctly.

(*) Except mine, but the productization of LSM and MP support in
V3 killed it off.

