I have had in the past microvax 2 systems both in 630 corp. cabinet and BA123 
config. Both have had KDA-50 and RA-82/RA72 drives on them with no problem.

I got in a MV3900 system in a BA123 cab. I moved the KDA-50 controller to the 
MV3900 and never mind the all-day "find-the-slot-that-works" game, once I did 
this, I thought everything was ok until I started noticing several fault 
light cycles on my otherwise good drives of which I had never had a fault 
light come on. The fault light would come on for a second, the port light 
would go out, and then they would both reset and go on with their life... 
trouble is that they trashed one of my RA-72 drives to the point that I guess 
