RB_Gray@ix.netcom.com wrote:
> 
> I have a DEC pc XL 590 with a NCR C810 SCSI Host Adapter built in to the
> mother board. Is there a way to upgrade the SCSI bios oe the drivers for
> this adapter ?
> 
> At one time I tried to upfrade the drivers but I could not see my hard
> drive afterwards.
> 
> Also there is a 1.23 system BIOS update on the DEC web site. It's ment
> for a 486 to pentium upgrade. Any advantage up upgrading my system from
> 1.22 to 1.23 ?

The NCR BIOS comes with the system BIOS. If my memory serves me right,
there was no NCR SCSI BIOS update in BIOS V1.23 (as compared to V1.22).

Technically, I suppose, you should be able to find the NCR BIOS in
the full BIOS image, and replace that (and only that ;-) with a newer
from http://www.symbios.com (or ftp://ftp.symbios.com), and then
flash with the "patched" ROM image.

If you don't know what you're doing, don't try it (and even if you
do, keep a "Crash Recovery Disk" at hand, because in all likelihood
you will need it before you get things working).

The above Symbios Logic sites also have the latest drivers (but they
don't help you much if there's a BIOS bug that needs to be overcome;
I don't know if there is, but I do know that NCR/Symbios has come
out with newer BIOS releases for the '810' than what's in the
DECpc XL BIOS 1.22/1.23).

My favourite approach: Use and Adaptec 2940* and disable the on-board
NCR. ;-)

