> Where do I find the PHLASH Utilities???
> I found a upgrade version for the starion 400/500 bios a file called
> BG90404A.EXE after expanding I'm afraid to run phlash.exe.
> ALL the documentation says "Create a crisis recovery diskette."
> 
> " HOW????  Without  a bakup of my old bios if the upgrade fails i'm
> SOL.
> 
> DEC  is no help.
> 
> marti@nac.net

It should all be documented in the User's Guide for the PC,
but nevertheless: copy the BIOS upgrade files to a new, empty
directory, have a formatted, empty diskette at hand, and
run MAKECRD.

When you do the BIOS upgrade, to be on the safe side, disable
all caching in CMOS SETUP and boot from a DOS diskette that
doesn't load any drivers (you could "SYS A:" the BIOS upgrade
floppy - if there's lack of space, remove BIOS images for
languages you're not going to flash the system to).

To repeat: Look in the User's Guide, it should be there 
(depending on the machine, it might exist only as an on-line
version, but most likely it is also in a booklet that
accompanied your PC).

regards,
