XESS Spreadsheet Updated with Enhanced Excel File Support


Chapel Hill, NC - April 28, 1997 - Applied Information Systems (AIS)
has released enhanced support for Excel files as part of version 3.1.3
of its award-winning XESS spreadsheet products.  This version will
ship to new customers and is an optional upgrade for existing users on
all supported Unix, OpenVMS, and Windows NT platforms. 

The enhanced Excel file support makes it much easier for XESS 
spreadsheet users to exchange spreadsheets with PC users.  XESS can 
now read files created by Excel versions 3, 4, 5, and 7 (Excel 95) and 
can write files is Excel 4 format.  XESS can also read and write 
Lotus file formats WKS, WK1, WK3, and WK4.  UNIX and OpenVMS 
users can now easily access spreadsheets sent to them by e-mail or
placed on Web servers.

"This enhanced file filter is based on work that is part of our 
extensive development for Xess97 which will be available later this 
year," said Arthur Coston, president of AIS.  "Because of the 
importance of maintaining compatibility with other products, we decided 
to include a version of the enhanced Excel file filter with this update."

XESS was the first commercial spreadsheet designed specifically for the 
X Windows and Motif environments and its inovative technology continues
to set the standard.  The XESS product family ranges from powerful personal 
spreadsheet products to advanced application development systems.  And 
all of these work on the widest range of platforms:
	SunOS  (SPARC)
	Solaris  (SPARC and Intel x86) 
	HP-UX (HP 9000)
	IRIX (Silicon Graphics)
	SCO UUNIX (Intel x86)
	Linux (Intel x86) 
	Digital UNIX (OSF/1) (Alpha AXP)
	Ultrix (DEC MIPS)
	OpenVMS (Alpha AXP)
	VMS and OpenVMS (VAX)
	DG/UX (Data General)
	AIX (IBM RS6000)
	Windows NT (Intel and Alpha)

More information on the XESS family of products and free evaluation 
versions are available through http://www.ais.com.  

Applied Information Systems, headquartered in Chapel Hill, North
Carolina, is a 24-year-old supplier of software products and
solutions.  It specializes in multi-vendor integration applications
and advanced client/server applications. 

