In article <335ede28.4134055@news.lightstream.net>, -- <--> wrote:
>Hello,

Hi...

>	Does anyone know of a parts store that carries the 10Base5 (
>ThickNet) AUI Terminator (15 pins)?   I have called and looked for
>this part in my area but I am having no luck in finding it.  

As far as I know, there's no such thing as an AUI terminator. The 
Application Unit Interface doesn't need termination. 

Could it be that you are looking for a transceiver for attaching to
a 10Base5 network? That would use an AUI cable to connect from the 
computer (or other device) to the cable. A terminator for a 10Base5
cable would be an N-series connector, not a 15 pin D-series.

The transceivers aren't common, but not too scarce either--I believe 
someone listed some in the net-hardware forsale group recently.


Gary


