This three tier nonsense gives me the creeps. Usually the "high tier" 
(OpenVMS) can perfectly well do everything the middle tier is supposed to
handle.  If there were any inexpensive OpenVMS machines left a single
cluster could easily be set up to handle all three tiers - with no single
point of failure on the server side.  The three tier architecture is
insanely complicated and only a company with a big MIS division would have
the resources to handle it.  For an example of three tiers, see this link
from the OpenVMS home page: 

