>...the regulator on the board would supply 3.3vdc if there wasn't a
>power supply hooked up to do it.

The regulator on the board supplies 3.3v for the CPU from the 5v
power supply regardless of whether or not you have a 3.3v power
supply attached to the motherboard. The 3.3v power supply connectors
power *only* the PCI slots. Unless you are using 3.3v PCI cards,
you do not need a 3.3v power supply for the AXPpci33.

