Hi,
There is a BIG problem with the write-back cache batteries on the HSZx0,
HSJx0, and HSDx0 family of controllers. It seems that the 5 year
batteries that the vendor sold to DEC and that DEC sold to us, the
public, are failing at 18 months or so, + or - a couple of months. If
you are running a RAID set, there is a timer that once a day checks the
status of the battery, and when the batteries are more than 18 months
old thay give a status of being bad, drops the raid sets and your dead
in the water, until you reboot the HSx. So, the recommendation is that
everyone who has these controllers should replace the batteries A.S.A.P.
with a set that has a Janurary 97 or later date on them. The Part # for
a set of batteries is 70-32162-01, and good luck on getting a set of
them. I just replace 6 sets on some HSD30 controllers and it took nearly
5 weeks to get all of the batteries replaced. It seems that this is a
nation wide problem that DEC is trying to keep quiet!

Replace your batteries and your problems should go away.

Needlessly to say, the above is pure opinion---and all the other stuff
that goes with it..
Tim



