I just measured the power consumption of my MicroVAX II in a BA123 (5
megs, 2 RD53, TK50, RX50).  It isn't too bad.  At startup it is almost 3
amps and when running it fluctuates around 2.22 amps (meaning 266 W). 
It still makes a good room heater for some reason.
However, one thing surprised me:  it uses about 60 milliamps (only 7.2
watts) when turned off from the front panel switch.  Flipping the
breaker takes that to zero.  Now I'm wondering is there any reason for
this?  Does it have any purpose such as charging the battery or keeping
exact time or is it just being wasted in the power supply.

I'm also wondering what is the purpose of the 3 pin female molex
connector which has only two pins and is located near the power cord
connector.

