william@ans.net writes:
> I am going to try to fetch a pair of these beasts soon, and have questions...

  Why?

> Does anyone have a decent estimate for their weight?

  They're on wheels (make sure the feet are adjusted all the way up first
before moving them). I've manhandled the drive part into the top of their
dedicated H9642-style cabinet myself, so they aren't *that* heavy (com-
pared to an RM02, let's say).

> How can I secure the heads for shipment?

  If the batteries aren't dead, these drives auto-park on spindown or loss
of power. There's a relay-operated catch, so the heads lock automatically.

  Note that RK07's require a special controller (RK611) which is only avail-
able for Unibus systems. It's a special 9-slot backplane (System Unit) and
most of them (especially if they've been in storage) have developed wire rot.
I actually had a few that we had completely cleared of wires and re-wrapped
about 5 years ago because the failures were so annoying, but these are long
gone now.

