> >
> >Just wanted to check and see if this is a known feature...
> >
> >My recent tests showed that if the SCSI adapter and SCSI disk support are
> >configured as modules, then on "power-on", the SCSI disks will not
> >"SPIN-UP".  Boot messages reports controller and disks found, but errors
> >reading the partition tables.
> >
> >If the SCSI adapter and SCSI disk support are compiled into the kernel,
> >then the disks DO "SPIN-UP" on "power-on".  Boot messages state "Spinning
> >up Disk" and disks are then mounted without errors.
> >
> >I've got a noname NCR 53c800 PCI SCSI adapter and 2 DEC RZ24 (okay, you can
> >laugh) disk drives and kernel 2.0.29.  The disks do not "SPIN-UP" by
> >themselves when power is applied.
> >
> >Just checking to find out if this was a module design limitation.
