>I was wondering what happens in a DEC Alpha multi-CPU box - running UNIX - 
>when one of the CPUs fails. If CPU 0 goes down, as this runs bits of the OS 
>I'd expect the box to fall over. But what about one of the other CPUs? Does 
>the box fall over? Does it do an automatic restart? Does it limp along on the 
>CPUs remaining without a reboot? I don't think there is any "fault-tolerance" 
>in the OS to allow restart of application processes running on the dead CPU.
>
