> BTW, are there any NT drivers available for ANY of the TLZ series of
> drives ?

The "generic" 4mm DAT driver usually works (except for the TLZ04, 
which requires a special driver, which will write tapes that can 
only be read by a machine with that driver and a TLZ04; so, if you
only have one TLZ04 and it breaks... ;-).

The TLZ04 driver has been on, at least, the DEC4WNT forum on
CompuServe. For the others, the driver is part of all Windows NT
kits (personally I have used TLZ06 & TLZ07 drives with Windows NT).

