I'm quite happy with my Zenith Z19 dumb terminal, rarely am I stuck using
a PC or Workstation.  However, I don't use my terminal standalone.  All
the functions listed above are functions of the host computer and work
much the same on a terminal as they do on a workstation.  I prefer the
terminal + computer because it separates the user interface hardware
from the compute hardware.  I also happen to dislike using a mouse for
text.

Disadvantages of the workstation include the long login time, noise
from fans and disks, and the requirement for a mouse.  Disadvantage
of a dumb terminal is a lack of on-screen real estate (though that
seems to be a marketing decision and has nothing to do with being
a dumb terminal).

I use the UNIX program "screen" to provide the sessions, scroll back,
cut and paste, and logging.  Since the screen program has much to offer
over "just a bunch of DECterm's", I suspect many workstations users
are running screen in a terminal window.



