In article <335209BE.74589321@usdesign.com>, Charles McCrobie <mccrobie@usdesign.com> writes:
> We have a Micro VAX II, CPU KA630-A.V1.3 Q-BUS machine.  I've looked at
> Digital's WEB pages and Alta-vista and found some suppliers of Q-BUS
> cards, but no "definitive" information as to the possible configurations
> of memory,
> ethernet, and graphics cards for Q-BUS machines.

Could you give a list of EVERY module installed in this machine so we can 
advise you a little better.
Starting at the CPU which we know that you do have (ie M7606-xx).

Normally you have 0/1/2 memory boards following the CPU connected to the 
CPU via a (50pin?)ribbon cable(sometimes shielded) .
Then follows your peripheral interfaces/adapter cards.
It would also help if you can tell which type of enclosure(thence backplane
type ) you have.
 Generally BA23(large oil heater size) or BA123(floor standing on castors)
for this vintage machine. (I have used BA11-S as well as BA213 enclosures 
to Kludge-up a quick and dirty test system at times)

> We have a Q-BUS card that I'm not sure what it does:
>         M7551-CA   memory module?  What machine does this work in?
>                    There are some switches.  Sorry, we don't have the
>                    manual for the board.  A manual would be welcome...
From fading memory is a 4MB Qbus memory(not KA630{MVII} PMI) which was used 
on PDP11/73/23(/53?) systems and also on the Microvax 1(? Kd32 ?).
This memory is not generally suitable for use with the MVII(ka630). 
 
> An attempt to install this board caused the MVII to BUGCHECK during
> BOOT.

Understandable as the KA630 maps the Qbus memory space(4MB) to the PMI memory
(16MB max) and you have a memory conflict because the Qbus memory is 
"getting in the way" of this mapping.
 
> The RX50 won't show up at SYSGEN AUTOCONFIG ALL.  In fact, at the
This type of command is not available from the chevron("sargent") prompt on 
this machine.

> sleeping sargent, B DUB0 and B DUB1 produces "DEVOFFLINE".  The
> controller does show up  as PUB0.  I believe the RX50 unit itself is
> broken.  Power to the unit  is good. 

Could you please post the results of  $ SHOW DEV/FULL D
 
> It appears that only two MS630-BB memory modules may be installed.  Am I
> correct is assuming the maximum memory for this machine is 8 (9) MB?  I
> have seen advertisements for 16 MB Q-BUS memory cards.  Will these work in

SEE BELOW

> the MicroVAX II and is it possible to install 3 such cards (in slots 2,3,
> and 4) for a total of 3*16 + 1 or 49 MB?

The KA630(cpu) can only connect to a maximum of two memory boards via the 
ribbon cable(only two memory buffer select lines signals on the cable).
The cpu is limited to 16MB of physically ADDRESSABLE memory(on the cpu 
there is a signal to allow memory sellection called LOW16MB). Even though 
you can install two MS630-CA(8MB ea) which gives you 17MB of SILICON MEMORY
, the CPU only decodes 16MB.

Regarding the advertised 16MB memory cards. These are probably MS650-series 
memories for the KA650/655 series of CPUs.
 These won't work with the KA630 cpu. 
The ribbon cable (BERG)connector on these is slightly offset to the ones
in the MS630 so that it is awkward to inadvertantly connect to the wrong
cpu type using the DEC cables. They use differnet signals and interconnect 
protocol on the cable also.
 
> I've seen DEQNA boards for this machine.  Are there any "got-chas" with
> the DEQNA and if so, what other Ethernet boards are available?

Try to lay your hands on a DELQA(-ya) = M7516? which will overcome some 
shortcommings in the DEQNA(m7504).(Sometimes says bad packets are good)
You can't use the DEQNA as a cluster interconnect as of VMS 5.4-3 and I'm 
sure ALL other support was discontinued well before V7.1 .
 
> Is it possible to get a graphics board for this machine?  I have NOT
> seen a
> graphics card advertised for this machine.  What would be the cost?

There were two "graphics" options that I know of 
VCB01	single plane monochrome(single board=M7602)
VCB02	4/8plane greyscale/colour(m7618/m7619? processor/memories)

> Would such graphics boards be supported under DEC Windows Motif 1.2-4

Check the SPD(Software Product Description)

> (if not, what software will support graphics boards for the machine?) 
> What type of monitor is required for above graphics boards?

Mono monitors VR260,VR150,...
ColoUr monitors VR290,VR299,VR160,... 

> Oh, we have OpenVMS 7.1 running on the machine now.  Installed and
> booted without a problem!

What are you using as a system disk?
The largest drive supported for the RQDX3=m7555(which also controls RX50)
was the RD54(159MB). I didn't think V7.1 would fit as people rarely took
this machine beyond 5.5-x unless they had RA- series drives(or third party
disks).(RX50 was also controlled by RQDX2/1=m8639-YB/00?)
 
> Just asking for information,
> Chuck McCrobie
> ** MAD VAX **

Just trying to help,
