You seem to want a vendor-independent RAID implementation.  Have you
looked into AUSPEX (it's bullet-proof) or Network Appliance?  Auspex
is easy to backup with dump/tar/cpio as a host processor runs SunOS 4.1.4.
NetApps are harder as they run their own OS which doesn't allow remote
login and a very limited unix command set.  It can do a unix dump to
attached tape robots which are seen as a stacker.  BudTools is the
only backup product which integrates well with NetApps currently.

