Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Hi:

> I have 2 RD53s with spin down disease.

I had this problem with one of my RD53s. Inspection revealed that the
drive was spinning down due to friction between the little pad on the
drive brake and the drive wheel itself. The drive would run for about 5
minutes and then spin down.

Take the electronics board off of the back of the drive and take a look
at the spring loaded gizmo with the brake pad on it. The other half of
the arm goes to the solenoid. When you first activate the drive there
should be about 1 mm clearance between the pad and the spinning drive
wheel. 

If there isn't then turn off the drive, and loosen the two screws
holding the solenoid down. Pull the solenoid unit back a bit and
re-tighten. Power up the drive and check clearance again. Redo until you
get proper clearance.

I have read that there can be other causes for RD53 spin-down, but this
worked for me, good luck.

Kevin

