Monday(!) I'm moving from a VAXStation 3100 M76 with VMS 5.2 which I've
always accessed with VT (clones---Ampex, Falco, Pericom) terminals to an
Alpha with VMS 7.1 and 17" colour monitor with DECWindows.  The years of
terminal work have set high standards for what I expect from a terminal
emulation, both with regard to display and with regard to the way keys
send what they're supposed to (even after being redefined, which,
however, was rarely needed on a good clone) which, at least with UNIX,
is a nightmare under X.  On a related note, I received the `standard VMS
keyboard' which has the number LK46W-A2 on the back. Of all the non-DEC
terminals, which were basically VT220 (at least that's the mode I
used---with 7 bits and no parity), I liked the Falco keyboard best.  I
hope I won't miss the escape key, the backspace and linefeed keys (the
second useful when telnetting to a UNIX system) and so on.  There are
enough keys on the Digital keyboard, but apart from the fact that I'll
have to get used to the name of the key not being printed on it, I'm
wondering if it is possible to reconfigure certain keys so that they
ALWAYS send another value.  I don't mean like F11-F13 which VMS
sometimes interprets as ESC, BS and LF (at least that's how I understand
it) but ALWAYS behave in a new way, whether at the command line, in EDT,
in some third-party application, when telnetting to a unix machine etc. 
The way it is on a REAL terminal.  Obviously I don't have much
experience in this area.  I'm looking for a way to do it ONCE to make it
valid EVERYWHERE, like on a terminal, and not redo it in each
application.  (Of course, if some application interprets these in a non-
ASCII way, that's a different matter of no concern at the moment.) 

Specifically, I would like the key to the left of 1/! to be `/~ (
probably the default) and not ESC.  ESC should be moved to the </> which 
is to the left of z/Z (< and > are SHIFT , and . so they're redundant 
here).  The ALT on the right should be LF and the COMPOSE on the right 
should be BS (I'm assuming that the ALT and COMPOSE on the left will 
give me all the functionality I need.

I had an X-terminal once with VTxxx keyboard which had `/~ on </> as an 
alternate, so one could use the upper left key as ESC.  Keys like `/~, 
which I use all the time in LaTeX, should have the value printed on the 
key, which is why I want it to be at upper left and ESC, which I rarely 
use, to be mapped to </>.

Something else---how can one use a serial terminal as the console of an
AlphaStation 255?  On the VAX you could connect to a serial port and
throw a switch or whatever (I've never actually done it myself, but have
seen it in action).  (I'm thinking of emergency situations here and not, 
at least not yet, of actually using the terminal instead of the monitor 
and keyboard I have bought.)

In case I'm not completely happy and would like to use another keyboard 
with the monitor, such as (one like a) Falco keyboard, is this possible 
or are they completely incompatible?  Does Digital manufacture any 
keyboard with the Falco VT layout?


