> 
> I can't find a way to monitor other user terminal screen. I have a
> system account. Is there a way to do it.

Yes, but how (and with what tools/products) depends very much on
what hardware platform and operating system we're talking about
(without going into the discussion of why you want to do it).

Given that this is comp.sys.dec, I presume you mean a hardware
platform and operating system from Digital Equipment Corporation,
but that doesn't get us very far (unless we limit ourselves to
current platforms - Alpha- and Intel-based Digital systems -
and operating systems, which means OpenVMS, Digital UNIX and
Windows NT, foremost). And since you mentioned "terminal",
I suppose Windows NT is ruled out.

If we have to consider older platforms (VAX, MIPS, PDP,
DEC-10/20) and operating systems (VMS, ULTRIX, RSX, RSTS,
TOPS-10/20 and whatnot), this gets more complicated (or then
maybe not ;-).

In any case, no operating system I've encountered on any 
Digital platform (covers about 11 years of Digital experience)
supports monitoring user terminals OOTB (out of the box); i.e.,
you do need to find specific tools/utilities for it.

Unfortunately, no matter how much I seem to be writing, no
actual product names are surfacing in my mind. ;-) Try 
searching for suitable keywords through

    http://altavista.digital.com/
    http://www.dejanews.com/
    etc.

