> the drive ! It still shows up (using Show Device DKA100:) but
> Initialize DKA100: DISK1 results in a dreadful "%INIT-F-DRVERR" !
> I can't see that there's a faulty drive 'cause this is the second drive
> I'm trying to install ! I've also tried the drive in a Mac and it works
> fine there.

The SCSI spec is somewhat "loose" and old VMS SCSI drivers were rather
particular to how well a drive conformed to its view of how a drive
should behave.  I think Quantums were notorious for failing this
test.

Newer (e.g. V7.1) VMS drivers are much more tolerant, important now that
Digital no longer makes its own SCSI drives.

-Mike



