OK. Let's stop teasing him.

You are correct. But so was the reply to your post. There
are no VMS binaries for the Intel platform to translate into
VMS binaries for the Alpha platform.

This is what FX!32 does. It converts Windows binaries which
have been compiled for the Intel platform to Windows
binaries which will run on the Alpha platform. The Windows
kernel for both platforms is very similiar (if not
identical)

You seem to want to run Windows binaries for the Intel
platform on VMS for the Alpha platform. The VMS kernel is
VERY different than the Windows kernel, therefore creating
the problem you are addressing. 

Linux and WindowsNT use generally the same basic kernel for
all of the different platforms it runs on, so conversion is
fairly straightforward. The VMS kernel does not run on Intel
processors at this point. I have heard of a port in the
works, but know nothing about it. Even then, it is not
likely that software manufacturers will port their software
to VMS just because it is not likely many people will be
using it.

I hope this clears this up for you.

Steven Underwood

