>         M7551-CA   memory module?  What machine does this work in?
>                    There are some switches.  Sorry, we don't have the
>                    manual for the board.  A manual would be welcome...
 

 M7551-CA     4MB PARRITY MEMORY FOR QBUS MSV11-QC

This is memory for a PDP11 (/73?).

> <SNIPPED>
> It appears that only two MS630-BB memory modules may be installed.  Am I
> correct is assuming the maximum memory for this machine is 8 (9) MB? I have
> seen advertisements for 16 MB Q-BUS memory cards.  Will these work in
> the MicroVAX II and is it possible to install 3 such cards (in slots 2,3,
> and 4) for a total of 3*16 + 1 or 49 MB?

 <SNIPPED>

Maximum memory for a MVII is 17Mb with two MS630-CA (8 Mb) memory
boards.
The 16Mb boards are probably for a MVIII, their type would be
MS650-BA/BF or
MS655.

MVII accesses it's memory through 50 pin ribbon cable, the Memory
Expansion Connector and the CD-connectors. The MVIII does the same but
it calls it the Private Memory Interconnect, the PDP11/73 uses the Q-bus
for it's memory accesses. All three are incompatible with each other.

