A Prioris HX6200 has already on on-board Ethernet controller that uses a
DC21142 chip.
The DE500-AA however has a DC21140 chip. Where the DC21140 is certainly
supported by Sun Solaris, I'm not sure about the newer DC21142 and DC21143
chips that we use today. (The latest version of the DE500, the DE500-AB
uses a 21143, where shortly also the HX machine will start using this
ship)
The on-board SCSI-controllers are indeed AIC-7880 controllers. Basically
the same as an Adaptec 3940UW. These are certainly supported by Sun
Solaris.
Maybe you want to start by making sure that Sun Solaris does not detect the
DC21142, and tries to load a driver that only supports up to the DC21140.
In theory there should be no problem with the AIC-7880 controllers.

Peter Bats
PCBU Server Support Engineering
Digital Equipment Corporation

PS: Officially we do not support Sun Solaris. Sun does however support our
hardware. Were it looks like that for some sort of reason the latest models
(HX6200/MX62000 and XL6200) are not on there list. However, each of these
systems uses standard components, like Mylex RAID controllers, Adaptec
AIC-7880 controllers, S3Trio32/64 video chips, and DC21x4x network chips
(like most of the networks boards do, except for 3-COM and Intel who use
their own chips, and some AMD based ones)


