Depends what is meant by that statement.  Clearly, Intel is lagging
further behind with respect to top-level performance, and the RISC chips
that have always outperformed their CISC chips are now starting to
compete in the same market -- with mainstream OS'es and applications.
At the same time, Cyrix and AMD have x86 clones as fast as Intel's high
end processors, but at a lower price.

On the other hand, Intel is standing on a *lot* of ground, and I suspect
that they get most of their revenue from other sources than their x86
CPU line (but I have no facts about this, of course.  This *is* Usenet,
you know).  Also, Intel made more money last year than just about
anybody else, and their CEO have the reassuring slogan that ``only the
paranoid survive''.  While not exactly lyrical, it might be sound
business sense.

