Gernot Bauer <org@skwb.co.at> writes:

> As far as I made the experience with DEC and Linux there is nearly NO
> support. I cant understand why because their PCs would be perfect for running
> Linux (and way faster than NT). But however there IS Linux knowledge at DEC,
> so lets tell them to jump onto the Linux-train!

As I understand it, DEC's model is to leave the Linux market to third-
and fourth-party vendors.  DEC Semiconductor has a couple of people
working on Linux/Alpha but no plans (AFAIK) to provide any end-user
support.  IMHO, it would be silly for them to try.

Fortunately, unlike in the x86 world, most (third-party) Alpha vendors
know about Linux and will happily provide systems with Linux
pre-installed.  A partial list of such vendors is available in the
Linux/Alpha FAQ:

	hhtp://www.azstarnet.com/~axplinux/FAQ.html

  --david
