You may want to examine the two drives to see whether there is any way
for the controller cable, (ribbon cable) to be installed on the drive
end incorrectly.  The cable itself will have a "polarity indicator" ( a
stipe on one edge of the ribbon cable or the other edge) which indicates
which one of the wires is wire number one of the approximetly 34 wires. 
You next want to check that the wire which is number one plugs into the
drive on the end of the drive connector which is labeled  1 or which has
some other indicator.  Most drives will have an arrow, a dot, or some
other indicator saying which end of the connector should have the
striped edge of the ribbon cable.  Most of the time if you connect the
the drive backwards, (or reversed), you will not damage the drive nor
the computer, but will have an indication which resembles a "no Power"
condition on the screen.  So, try to ensure that the drive is connected
correctly into the computer.  And good luck!!



