This letter is to drum up support by end users to convince Hash that it is
worthwile to continue DEC Alpha Windows NT development. I post this to the 
newsgroup for general information.

This brings up a question. What developer support is available from DEC and 
how is DEC working with developers to start and continue Alpha NT ports?

Thanks,

Ed 

-------

To All,

If you are interested in the Animation Master(AM) and would like to see its
development continue on the fastest (>600mhz), most powerful (SPECfp95=27)
Windows NT platform, the DEC Alpha, please read the following.

Hash Inc. has decided not to port the upcoming V5 release of AM to the DEC
Alpha Windows NT platform due to low sales of V4. Hash is interested in
continuing Alpha NT work and has offered to port V5 if there is enough users
to make it financially sound. 

What is needed is for a minimum of 100 people to prepay for a V5 Alpha NT
version. This minimum is to be split into 50 new purchases ($699) and 50
current users to upgrade ($99). 

Zero at the 3D Ark web site has put up a page to list the people committed
to purchasing V5 for Alpha NT. The page is at:

http://scozone.com/3dark/hashfaqs/hashalpha.html

To show your commitment, and add your name to the AM V5 Alpha NT list,
send a email to: 

hashalpha@scozone.com

with the following information:

Name, E-Mail, Profession, Current Platform, Upgrade/Sidegrade or Purchase,
Quantity.

History:
Animation Master and the only dedicated 3D character animation package
other than Softimage (>$6000) on the Alpha NT platform. Version 4 is
currently supported on DEC Alpha Windows NT. Version 5 is a major upgrade
toward, if not surpassing, Softimage in character animation. More
information on V4 and the upcoming V5 can be found at http://www.hash.com

DEC Alpha information can be found at

http://www.digital.com/info/semiconductor/alpha.htm

If you have any questions about the above, you can contact me directly at
stutz@sonic.net

Thank you,

Ed




