I have an Alpha with turbochannel (a 3000-300lx). Its memory is ordinary
parity 72 pin SIMMs, 70ns or better. It can take either 8mb SIMMs or
32MB SIMMs. I doubled the memory I had by buying SIMMs from a cheap PC
parts supplier (made sure they were faster than 70ns...in fact their
cycle time was 50 ns). As long as you get parity parts they're fine. So
much for the theory that this memory was non standard.

