Reply-To: leinberger@axp621.gsi.de (Uwe Leinberger GSI Darmstadt)
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



As said very often here and to be found in the FAQ, VaxStation3100 
firmware (or BIOS in PCish terms) only knows how to handle disks up to 
1.073GB (ie can only address so-and-so many bits).

This means that the SYSTEM disk MUST be below this limit, otherwise you are 
bound to get in deep trouble.

However, all non-system disks can be as large as ~8.5GB on older VMS verions,
and larger since VMS6.0.

Uwe



