In article <334D9E6F.A9@dial.pipex.com>,
NATS Airport Systems <nats.airport.systems@dial.pipex.com> wrote:

> Today I tried to put a new 1.2GB Quantum drive onto a 3100 running
> VMS5.5-2.  I believe the firmware was KA42 v1.6 - about 5 years old.

First, the VS3100 console cannot deal with any drive greater than 1.073GB
in size as a system disk. (data disks can be any size the OS can handle -
5.5-2 is itself limited to 8.5GB, 6.0 and later 1TB)

> The bootstrap '>>>' prompt seemed to recognise it OK as a generic SCSI
> drive, but I couldn't initialise it, reporting errors such as :
> BACKUP-F-ALLOCFAIL - File Structure Allocation Failure for dka300:
> SYSTEM-F-DRVERR - Fatal Drive Error

The early VMS scsi drivers were very picky about which disk drives it would
talk to. Many non-DEC drives had firmware that would upset the VMS drivers.
V7.1 is much better regarding this.  I do not know whether their is any sort
of kit for 5.5-2.

> I've only used drives up to 450MB on 3100's before - does anyone know of
> any problem using larger disks - or is it just a problem with the drive
> / cabling / system configuration - or me being stupid.

The 1.073GB limit on the system disk size mentioned earlier.  Does not apply
to data disks.

-Mike



