Word is that MetaTools is releasing an Alpha-native
version (for NT) of Bryce 2, their 3D rendering package.

For those unfamiliar with the company, MetaTools is a
mainstream Mac/PC graphics-software house. They're probably
best known for the Photoshop plugin suite Kai's Power Tools,
and they've been getting into 3D in a big way.
 
MetaTools just bought Specular Software (Infini-D) and they're
planning a merger with Fractal Design Corp. (Fractal Design
Painter and Ray Dream Designer)

MetaTools is the kind of PC company that Alpha needs to quiet
folks who say "Alpha's fast, but there's no software for it."
 
If Bryce sales are solid on Alpha, we might be able to
look forward to Painter, Ray Dream, and Infini-D. And if
Painter goes Alpha native, Adobe might follow with Photoshop,
and then....

	-doug



