In article <334AF9D5.778D@acd.net>, "James D. McComb" <mccomb.james@acd.net> writes:
|>I am trying to attach a modem to the synchronus port of a DSH32-B in a
|>3100 20e.  However, I cannot find any doc. on how to configure it, other
|>drivers that may be required, or even the device name for the port.
|>
|>Any help or direction would be appreciated.
|>


What OS are you running? If it's OpenVMS, you need a set of drivers
to get the port working. For DECnet Phase IV you need, as a minimum,
WANDD V1.2A; if you are running DECnet-Plus (formerly DECnet/OSI) then 
the WANDD stuff is already included (assuming you asked for it to
be installed) but you will need a licence.

Once you get going the device name will be ZSA0:.

