The old (late '70s, early '80s) Microcomputer Interfaces handbooks from DEC
include the LSI-11 bus specification.

To save time getting something working, an alternative would be something like
an MDB-1710 that has the bus logic and a prototype (wire wrap) area.  DEC uses
a VLSI chip to implement the bus; maybe you can buy them.

