bagibson wrote:
> 
> I have aquired a digital desktop pc lpv+ 425sx which has been protected by
> a power on password. How do I disable this feature. I looked at the mother
> board and can find no battery to disconnect, nor can I find a jumper
> labelled "pswd reset"! How is the CMOS powered and how can I disconnected
> it?

The battery is combined with the RTC (real-time clock). It should be
pretty close to the connectors from the power supply to the motherboard
(if my memory serves me right).

It is probably a black, labeled square thing (most likely labeled
"Dallas" or "Rayovac", possibly "Benchmarq", etc.). It connects to
a 3- or 4-pin connector with a black and red wire (connecting just
the first and last pins).

