Organization: Transaction Technology, Inc.
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.graphics.apps.lightwave


Recently I got a DPW 433a.  I'm using it to run LightWave 3D 5.0.
Instead of getting one of Digital's graphics options, I went with
Dynamic Picture's Oxygen 202.

One thing I noticed right away is the slow response of the command
prompt window (yes, I perfer typing commands over using the mouse).
Scrolling through a directory is rather slow.  And while typing in
a command, I could see the typed characters being refreshed (they
flicker).

Another thing is, the OpenGL screen saver maze is also much slower
on the 433a than a typical 200Mhz Pentium system.

The Pentium that I used to compared has less RAM (32 vs 64 megs),
Matrox Millenium (2 megs vs Oxygen's 16 megs), slower CPU
(obviously), same OS level (NT 4.0, sp2), same graphics resolution
(1024x768), and more colors (64k vs 32k).

What can I attribute such a poor graphics performance to?

Some possibilities that I came up with are:
1. Inefficient code in command prompt window.
2. Oxygen 202 has poor 2D performance.
3. Bugs in BIOS, drivers.
4. Poor PCI bus throughput.

Anyway, I appreciate any help on this matter.  Thanks.

Jack



