"Dennis Moran" <coolio@coolio9.com> writes:
> I'm not sure. It will most likely increase performance on the other Alphas,
> but a different proportion. Still, I find it amazing that Digital can run
> software that's written for a totally different architecture, and make it
> run twice as fast as the fastest processor from Intel using *software
> emulation*...
--

Whiy is this amazing? The PentiumPro converts IA32 instructions into
RISC micro-ops on the fly. The PPro instruction fetch & decode
stage is very long (~6-7 cycles) to make this happen.

I don't see much difference in doing it via software translation (what
FX!32 does) and hardware translation (PPRO), except that the software
method hasn't been exploited for drivers and the like.




