>>I bought two AXP pic33 motherboards with a 21066 processor and it is 
>>supposedly "new". I have a SVGA card in one of the ISA slots and 8meg 
>>of ram. When I power it up nothing happens. I downloaded the firmware 
>>update off of digital's web page. I put that on a disk and tried to boot 
>>off of that and all that happens is the disk light is always on and the 
>>drive spins when I put the disk in.
	IF the floppy disk light comes on imemdiately on power up its a problem.
	IN General, it means the floppy disk cable is in 'backwards'.  It turns
	out that people build floppy disk cables both ways, so sometimes the
	drive end has to be put in 'against' the keying.  USUAL symptom of
	this is the floppy drive light coming on immediately (and the drive not
	being usable).  I've never seen this damage either drive or control,
	but I'd get that floppy drive sorted first.

	Also, floppy drive should be after ONE twist in the cable: depending
	on how the cable was built this could be the first or second connetor.
	first or second is not important, being after 'one twist' is.

	I'd:
	1) get the floppy drive light out.
	2) get in at least 16 MB of 'real parity' simms.
	3) get some life on the console before trying toi do FW upgrade.
	(checking for activity on the serial port is a step this way...)

>> Other than that there is no activity even from the speaker (Im not sure if
>there is supposed to be any at this point).
	Typically not.

