This is just a remainder of the existence of NetBSD/vax, for those of you
who want to play with something else than VMS/Ultrix.

NetBSD is a fully operational 4.4BSD-based operating system that are 
running on many different platforms; among them are the DEC VAX.

Among the VAX CPU types that are supported are:

VAX 11/780 - 11/785
VAX 11/750
VAX 8600/8650
MicroVAX II/III/3600/3800/3900
MicroVAX 3200/3300/3400/3500 with Q-bus.

Work are currently being done on MicroVAX 2000 and the different
flavours of MicroVAX 3100.

For more information about this you may want to check the web pages at
http://www.netbsd.org/Ports/vax and the NetBSD/vax FAQ at
http://www.bitcon.no/~gunnar/vaxbsd/FAQ.html.

If you still have questions after looking at this they can be
directed to me directly: ragge@netbsd.org.

Good luck!

-- Ragge
