   Synopsis: The DCE DCE$DTSD time service daemon may fail
             to start after 6-Apr-1997.

   Remedy:   Install the VAXLIBR06_070 and/or ALPLIBR05_070
             ECO kit.

       Product:
         Distributed Computing Environment (DCE) for OpenVMS
	   versions V1.3A to V1.4

       Operating System:
         OpenVMS VAX
           versions V5.5-2 to V7.0
         OpenVMS Alpha
           version V6.1 to V7.0
           
   The Distributed Computing Environment (DCE) package is a seperately-
   installed DIGITAL software product for OpenVMS.

   The daylight savings time change-over may cause the DCE time service
   daemon, DCE$DTSD, to fail to start.  (The switch to daylight savings
   time will typically occur in the early morning hours of 6-Apr-1997
   in most parts of the United States.)

   After the daylight savings time change-over, the DCE$DTSD daemon
   may fail to start, and may write the following error message to
   the DCE$DTSD.OUT file:

    "Fatal error at line 782 in file decw$dceresd:[dts.src]timers.c;1"

   This event is associated with the DCE$DTSD daemon referencing a time 
   value after the 19-May-1997 10K delta-time "threshold", via a call to
   a pthread (DECthreads) routine covered by the 10Kday delta-time ECO.

   This DCE$DTSD error and the underlying delta-tine problems are resolved
   by the 10Kday delta-time VAXLIBR06_070 (OpenVMS VAX) and ALPLIBR05_070
   (OpenVMS Alpha) ECO kits.

   For information on reviewing application code, for testing procedures,
   for the current 10Kday delta-time Questions and Answers (Q&A), and for
   copies of the ECO kits, please see URL http://www.openvms.digital.com.

