Some implementations of tagged queueing don't really work as VMS expects...
VMS uses all 256 legal tags (though it does not expect or require that
a drive allow that many queued operations). However, there seems to be
some incompatibility with some drive firmware, exact nature not known to
me.

If that's going on, setting the disable tagged queueing bit in the
drive would let vms 7.1 work; it checks this.

The bit is in the control mode page of the device, page code
0Ah (10 decimal). The low bit of byte 3 (counting from zero) of the
page is DQUE. If it is set to 1, thedrive won't do tagged queueing.
(Leave other bits alone there...).

If the drive in question won't allow the bit to be changed, you need
to muck around with dkdriver tables in completely unsupported ways. The
RIGHT way to deal with this is to file a call with official support.
Email or news groups don't get any engineering time allocated. Support
calls CAN do that.
Glenn Everhart



