In article <E84vzu.6zC@novice.uwaterloo.ca>,
David Evans <dfevans@bbcr.uwaterloo.ca> wrote:
>  Suppose I want to have both an RX50 and an RX33.  Assuming I set the CSRs
>properly, can I just stick in a second RQDX3 and put a second signal
>distribution board above the first one?  It looks like NetBSD/vax can handle
>multiple RQDX3s (it handles my single one now plus another emulating
>controller) so the software side sounds fine.

Yep, it'll work fine.  I had three RQDX3s in a uVAX II without any trouble;
I currently have two RQDX3s plus a third-party MSCP ESDI controller (along 
with all sorts of other junk) in a dual-BA23 configuration.

The RQDX3 doesn't use any of the distribution panel signals for floppy
drives, so adding a second distribution board should be fine if you can
make it fit (I don't have any real experience with the BA123).  

Fixed disks prefer to have the online signal pulled up -- sometimes it
works without, sometimes it doesn't.  I had no trouble with an RD52
installed in the second hard disk position with only a BA23 four-button
panel (really a six-button one but with the components for the second
fixed disk controls missing), but an RD53 in the same hole wasn't keen.

-- 
