>  I have just installed Unix on my Alpha system. I am trying to
> register and load the OSF-USR (1050 user) license pak, and
> everything appears to procede smoothly. But, when a user tries
> to telnet into the system a message appears stating that too
> many users are logged-in. The console log shows that the OSF
> USR-BASE PAK cannot be found.
> 
>  Is this, USR-BASE PAK, a seperate module that has to be purchased or
> should it have come installed when I loaded Unix on my system?
> 
>  Any help would be appreciated.
> 
> -------------------==== Posted via Deja News ====-----------------------
>       http://www.dejanews.com/     Search, Read, Post to Usenet

The OSF-BASE PAK (is this the one you mean?) is the one that shows you
have a DIGITAL UNIX license. If you bought the system with D.U. I would
expect you to have a OSF-BASE license PAK. If you originally bought
the system with VMS or WNT, you won't - and you would need to purchase
the OSF-BASE license to be legally entitled to use DIGITAL UNIX.
Since you have a OSF-USR PAK, it sounds like you bought the system with
D.U. - in which case check your paperwork again, or contact your
supplier.

Regards,
John Hill
