>
>Ok hardware boys,
>
>I have a tape that refuses to eject from the TF85 drive buried deep in the
>TF857 hopper internals.
>
>I have tried the usual power off/on tricks but there is no way to persuade the
>hopper door to release.
>
If the drive is anything like the TK50 or TZ30 tape drive, the most
common problems I've sen on these that cause this problem are

1. The hook that pulls in the tape breaks. Pull apart the tape drive
   and replace the hook. They cost about $1 from DEC.
2. The leader on the front of the cartridge (the leader with the eye)
   comes unstuck. Pull apart the tape drive so you can get access
   to the front of the tape, scotch tape the leader back on (It's a
   real challenge), then the tape drive can be powered up and the
   tape removed.
3. (2) happens, and the tape drive gleefully does a (1) with the loose
   leader.

If your not mechanically inclined, I'd advise against trying to fix it
yourself. To properly do it involves lots of cussing and a set of
bloody knuckles.

