In article <33420287.2B22@rt66.com>, sleung@rt66.com <sleung@rt66.com> wrote:
>Does anybody know if an RQDX3 will work with a KDF-11BA cpu card ?
>(cpu rom rev 0.9. and cards in a BA-23 enclosure)

Yes, it will work.  If your ROM's don't have the DU boot code,
you'll either have to boot off another device and then use the
OS handlers to boot from the RQDX3, or you can stuff the boot
code in via console ODT and go from there.  For bootstraps, see

 http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/bootstraps

There's also the issue of operating system compatibility.  Whatever
OS you're using will obviously need the DU device handler.

>I have been using my LSI-11/23 with a pair of RL02 disk pack-drives.
>
>The RL02's are OK, but are noisy, big, and power hungry.
>
>I would like to use an RD-series drive internally in the cpu box.\

You'll very likely find that RD-series MFM hard drives aren't as
reliable as your RL02's. 

>It would be nice to have RX-50's instead of RX-02's, too.

Even better, use RX33's (1.2 Meg 5.25" HD floppies.)  You won't
be stuck with the infernal mechanics of the RX50, and you also
will be able to format your own floppies without resorting to
PC-clone tools like Teledisk.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



