Hi,
I tried to connect a SyQuest SQ555 removable hard disk drive to SCSI bus of my
DECstation 5000/xxx (MIPS-based).
First I read all the information given in
/sys/data/scsi_data.c
/sys/data/cam_data.c
and
/sys/h/devio.h

and created a new entry in cam_data.c to recognize the new device. As I guessed
there have to be new entries in scsi_data.c because SQ555 has removable media
which could not be given in cam_data.c. So I made a new entry in scsi_data.c.
Also I added a partition table (because only 44 MByte cap). Setting up SQ555 as
SCSI 0 and compiling the kernel should give no errors.
Well, booting the box the kernel said:

cam error bus 0 target 0 lun 0
Flushing residual bytes from FIFO
sim94_sel

After booting the first try to mount the device the same error appears in the
xconsole window but after that everything goes ok. Formatting (rzdisk -f)
partitioning (chpt -p) and creating filesys is possible. But sometimes the SCSI
bus hung and so did the box.

Is there anyone who has ever tried to connect such a device type to the SCSI bus
on a DEC MIPS box?
What about the entries in cam_data.c/scsi_data.c? What should I ask the vendor
(in this case SyQuest) about the SCSI features supported by the device? How do I
input them in the various kernel sources?

I really want to use this type of device, because it would hold all the measured
data I'm working on at home and at the office.

Any hints appreciated !

Uwe



